# Line endings
#
# Repository content is LF, and working trees stay LF on every platform.
# `eol=lf` overrides a contributor's `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows
# default), which would otherwise check files out as CRLF and strip them
# back to LF on commit.
#
# This matters beyond tidiness: the cross-implementation test vectors in
# vectors/ are the project's interoperability contract, and several are
# hashed or compared byte-for-byte. A CRLF round-trip on a vector file
# changes its bytes and would fail a conformance run for reasons that have
# nothing to do with the implementation under test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be transformed. Phase 1 adds compiled artifacts
# and docs may gain diagrams; declaring these up front avoids corruption
# if `text=auto` ever guesses wrong.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.jar  binary
*.der  binary
